-- ------------------------------------------------------------------ Coop: secret bases (Ruby / Sapphire / Emerald)
-- The base of each player (secretBases[0] of the save block, 160 bytes) is sent to the partner in 8 parts of 21 bytes (SBAS: part
-- number, 42 hex digits). The partner stores it as a base of another trainer in the first free slot (or in the slot that holds
-- that trainer's base already), so the game shows it like a base that came with a record mix: the entrance of the base is there
-- when the map is loaded, and the base can be entered. A base is sent again when it changed (decorations, party).
MPBaseOffset = {E = 0x1A9C, RS = 0x1A08}

